{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nRecord the approved RP-04 architecture before implementation. The completed research and probes live on `relevant-liberal-xantus` and in `.joe-janitor/rp04-secrets-research.md`, `.joe-janitor/rp04-composition-readback.md`, and `.joe-janitor/rp04-adr-research-critique.md`. This child is documentation-only and must not start RP-04 implementation.\n\n## Deliverable\nCreate ADR 0098, `docs/adr/0098-operation-scoped-config-and-provider-composition.md`, using this repository's ADR format and generator. The ADR records one coherent decision: Rebar composes immutable non-secret operation configuration with separately owned provider-auth/runtime bindings at application boundaries. The slug deliberately avoids the generic word `bindings`, which the generated index classifies under the reconciler workstream before it sees `config`; this keeps the application-wide decision in the Config & CLI index section.\n\n## Plan\n1. Work from a fresh worktree at current `origin/main`; reserve ADR 0098 with the generated `.numbers/0098` marker.\n2. Cite the completed primary-source and maintained-OSS research for Pydantic/PydanticAI, OpenAI, Anthropic, boto3/AWS, Git credential helpers/SSH, Jira integrations, CI secret injection, subprocess environments, and Rebar's current probes. Claims about dependency behavior must point to the exact source consulted.\n3. Describe the current split authorities, trust boundaries, behavioral regressions, and why configuration and authentication are related at composition time but remain separate data/capability models.\n4. Record the approved decisions: operation snapshot precedence/root rules and lifecycle; CLI/MCP/Python/service composition ownership; subsystem projections; provider-native pre-client auth/session injection into Rebar-owned factories; provider-specific `SecretStr`/`SecretBytes` static carriers; no universal secret broker/keyring/cloud-secret retrieval; subprocess environment rules without global mutation; restart/redeploy static rotation; SDK-owned refresh; fail-closed decision-bearing auth; and the optional observability exception.\n5. Record op-cert startup composition: exactly one path or multiline value, validation before service work, process-owned 0700/0600 copy, context-local signer/principal/push policy, no application runtime SSM/boto3/region coupling, and deployment freedom to retain SSM-at-rest before injection. Amend only ADR 0049's per-job retrieval/composition detail; preserve its algorithm, trust-root/era, producer, and deployment storage choices.\n6. Explain alternatives and rejection grounds: current ambient/per-consumer loading; one secret-provider/string lookup; application-owned SSM/keyring layer; aggressively restricted child environments; global `os.environ` overlays; public constructed-client/runner replacement; per-job op-cert retrieval; and hot rotation owned by Rebar.\n7. State security limits/non-goals, migration and rollback, compatibility effects, explicit behavior changes, observability/provenance constraints, and implementation verification obligations. Relate ADRs 0008, 0014, 0041, 0046, 0049, 0050, 0059, and 0083 without claiming to supersede their unaffected decisions.\n8. Regenerate `docs/adr/README.md` and `.numbers/0098`; make the minimal `docs/architecture.md` update appropriate for a proposed decision under this project's conventions.\n9. Run ADR-number/index/docs checks. Then perform and publish the required numbered Draft Critique: uncited claims, internal inconsistencies, missing constraints, and conflicts with existing ADRs. Resolve any mechanical/document defects, but stop before HOLD/MERGE and request explicit maintainer approval.\n\n## Verification\n- `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check`\n- `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py`\n- The repository's documentation/lint checks applicable to changed files.\n- Deterministic searches confirm no placeholder sections or merge-conflict markers in the changed ADR artifacts.\n- Read the rendered diff against the approved research and every related ADR named above.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] ADR 0098 exists in project-native format and accurately records the approved operation-snapshot, provider-auth/runtime-binding, subprocess, rotation, failure, observability, and op-cert decisions.\n- [ ] Every external dependency/OSS behavior claim has a specific primary or repository research citation; Rebar probe claims cite the recovery artifacts or durable research ticket.\n- [ ] Alternatives, consequences, security limitations/non-goals, explicit behavior changes, migration, rollback, and post-cutover compatibility are concrete enough that implementation stories need not invent architectural policy.\n- [ ] The ADR narrows ADR 0049 only at the per-job retrieval/composition seam and explicitly preserves all unaffected decisions; relationships to ADRs 0008, 0014, 0041, 0046, 0050, 0059, and 0083 are consistent.\n- [ ] `docs/adr/README.md` and `docs/adr/.numbers/0098` are generator-produced, collision-free, and pass their checks; `docs/architecture.md` points readers to the proposed decision without overstating implementation status.\n- [ ] The numbered Draft Critique is recorded on this ticket and identifies or explicitly clears uncited claims, inconsistencies, missing constraints, and ADR conflicts.\n- [ ] No RP-04 production code or implementation child stories are created, and the change remains in DRAFT/HOLD pending explicit maintainer authorization."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786991896577625001,"uuid":"e33a2caa-a0b2-4777-b984-8a1d079179e5"}